{"type": "plan", "agent": "lead", "reasoning": "Cantilever tip load: M = PL, sigma = 6PL/(b h^2), tip deflection = 4PL^3/(E b h^3). The governing case is REQ-006 (P = 2750 N, thickness h - 0.5 mm). Allowables are the lower of yield/1.25 and ultimate/1.6: Al 6061-T6 193.75 MPa, Ti-6Al-4V 593.75 MPa, Steel 4130 348 MPa. Deflection under the REQ-006 load limits stiffness (Ti and Al are deflection-limited). Screening stock thicknesses with width >= thickness/2 (REQ-007) gives a rough minimum area of about 450 mm^2 for Al (30 x 15, about 1.2 kg/m), about 240 mm^2 for Ti (20 x 12, about 1.06 kg/m), and about 325 mm^2 for Steel (25 x 13, about 2.55 kg/m). Ti-6Al-4V is the lightest candidate, with tip deflection of about 2.98 mm, which is tight against REQ-003.", "notes": {"Al 6061-T6": "Allowable is governed by ultimate, 310/1.6 = 193.75 MPa, which requires b(h-0.5)^2 >= 11,923 mm^3 and stiffness requires b(h-0.5)^3 >= 146,000 mm^4. Search thickness 20-30 mm with width near h/2; the best feasible point is about 30 x 15 mm (450 mm^2, about 1.2 kg/m).", "Ti-6Al-4V": "Stiffness, not strength, governs because E is 113.8 GPa and the allowable is 593.75 MPa; this requires b(h-0.5)^3 >= 88,400 mm^4. Search thickness 16-25 mm with width 12-24 mm; the best feasible point is about 20 x 12 mm (240 mm^2, about 1.06 kg/m) with deflection near 2.98 mm.", "Steel 4130": "Yield allowable 435/1.25 = 348 MPa is the tightest strength limit, requiring b(h-0.5)^2 >= 6,640 mm^3, and the high density of 7850 kg/m^3 penalises mass. Search thickness 16-25 mm with width 13-28 mm; the best point is about 25 x 13 mm (325 mm^2, about 2.55 kg/m), which is unlikely to win."}, "round": 1, "t": 21.94}
